% Obligation: (x << 1) >> 1 == x & 0x7fffffffffffffff, for every 64-bit word x.
% `>>` in Bebop is LOGICAL, not arithmetic (`>>>` is arithmetic) -- the inverse of
% the C convention, and the fact ROADMAP F9's theorem statement is false without.
% This is that fact as a machine-checked obligation rather than a comment: if
% bb_lshr64 sign-extended, the left-hand side would be x for every negative x and
% the right-hand side would still have bit 63 clear, so the certificate could not
% exist. 0x7fffffffffffffff = 2^63 - 1 = 9223372036854775807.
obligation lshr_is_logical
1 var x
2 shl 1 1
3 lshr 2 1
4 const 9223372036854775807
5 and 1 4
6 eq 3 5
prove 6
